---
List resource instances of a given type within a project.

Fetches the actual data instances stored in DSP for a resource-type. Supports single-page (`--page N`) and all-pages (`--all`) modes. Authentication is optional; anonymous callers see only public resources.

See also: dsp docs concepts

Usage: dsp vre resource list [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -s, --server <SERVER>
          DSP server URL or shortcut (e.g. `https://api.example.org` or `prod`). Can also be set via the `DSP_SERVER` environment variable or a `.env` file
          
          [env: DSP_SERVER=]

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (-v=info, -vv=debug, -vvv=trace). RUST_LOG overrides

  -p, --project <PROJECT>
          Shortcode, shortname, or IRI of the project

      --resource-type <RESOURCE_TYPE>
          Name or full IRI of the resource-type to list instances of. A bare name triggers a scan across all project data-models; use `--data-model` or a full IRI (`://` heuristic) to skip the scan

      --data-model <DATA_MODEL>
          Name or IRI of the data-model to scope the resource-type search. Optional; narrows the bare-name scan to one data-model

      --page <PAGE>
          Page number to fetch (zero-based). Cannot be combined with `--all`. Defaults to page 0 when neither `--page` nor `--all` is given

      --all
          Fetch all pages until the server reports no more results. Cannot be combined with `--page`

      --filter <FILTER>
          Filter resources by case-insensitive substring over the label

      --order-by <ORDER_BY>
          Field name (e.g. `title`) or full field IRI to sort by (ascending). A bare field name is resolved to the resource-type's field IRI; a full IRI (contains `://`) is passed to the server verbatim. Targets project-defined fields; ascending order only

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (default: prose)

          Possible values:
          - prose: Rich human-readable prose output with contextual hints (default)
          - json:  Newline-delimited JSON (one object per line)
          - lines: One identifier per line, for shell pipeline consumption
          - csv:   Comma-separated values with a header row
          - tsv:   Tab-separated values with a header row
          
          [default: prose]

  -j, --json
          Shortcut for --format=json

  -l, --lines
          Shortcut for --format=lines

      --columns <COLS>
          Output columns for tabular formats (csv, tsv, lines): comma-separated list that selects and reorders columns. Valid names are listed in the Columns line below. Duplicates are rejected

      --no-header
          Omit the csv/tsv header row, e.g. appending rows to an existing file

      --header-only
          Emit only the csv/tsv header row, no data rows. Note: the command still contacts the server

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Columns (--columns): label, iri, ark_url, creation_date, last_modified, resource_type

Scan behaviour: a bare --resource-type name (no ://) scans all project data-models; use --data-model or a full IRI to skip the scan. See also: `dsp docs concepts`

--order-by: field name (e.g. title) or full field IRI; sorts ascending; targets project-defined fields (full IRI passed verbatim; bare name resolved to its field IRI)
